Hello, thought I'd open with a YASD post...

Okay, so getting bored (and making little headway) with rogues, I
decide to play with some of the other classes.  After fun with wizards
and tourists, I decide to try monks, wow!  For some reason something
clicked, a class that's supposedly on the difficult side proved
extremely easy for me.

So Lucy the monk (3rd iteration thereof) is going sweet, gets down to
sokoban, wins a Bag of Holding, starts collecting junk (mainly orc
detrius, messy bastards they are) from various caches, transporting it
to stores and selling it.  By this time I'm feeling purty good; tenth
level, lots of food, lots of gold, decent AC and a few nice wands. I'm
not seriously thinking about ascension, I /am/ however considering the
Quest levels as realistic (a /big/ thing for me).

Then it happens, i foul up my prayer timeout, make my god angry. 
Okay, it's not too bad, he's only displeased, sacrifices will get
things back on track.  Anyway, since I'm on the 11th dungeon level and
have seen only a lawful altar thus far(Lucy being neutral), I decide
to try Minetown.  Lucy's tuff, the Dwarven Mines should be quite
doable for a Student of Stones.  Btw, did I mention the thousands of
zorkmids i've collected?  I figure if i'm hoping for a neutral altar
in minetown, might as well give lots of lucre to the priest; i might
get something nice.  :)

So back up to level 4 and down into the mines.  It's like i thought,
no serious challenge for a monk whose hand to hand skill is "Master,"
gnomes and dwarves crumple at my touch.  Then, on level 3 of the
mines, there's a leprechaun; it wakes up, steals about 3000 zorkmids
and runs off.  "Damn you, no-one steals from Lucy the monk.  My order
/values/ possessions, we're not like those pacifistic Tibetan
paupers."  I give chase, right back up into the regular dungeon.

A looonnnnng game of cat and mouse ensues; i run about like a mad nut,
the leprechaun teleports away.  Blindfolding myself and tracking him
via telepathy makes things easier, orcs start swarming and die by the
dozen for getting in my way.  After several near misses I'm no longer
thinking straight, Lucy loses her centre and starts dreaming of
genocide scrolls.  At one point i seriously consider heading down to
11 where there's a throne room; overkill i decide, but promise myself
leprechauns /will/ be first when the opportunity presents.  So i
continue chasing, at one point i (a)pply a mattock to a few key
junctions, makes circumnavigating a pair of floating eyes /much/
easier.  This was a mistake. . .

By this stage in the game i'm pretty worked up, the red haze has
fallen i forget that (a)pply with something weaponish also (w)ields
it. Without realising it, i blow the "never struck with a wielded
weapon" voluntary challenge and greatly reduce my chances to hit. So
eventually i corner the leprechaun, but am also cornered by a fire
ant.  So intent am i on getting my zorkmids back, i fail to notice i'm
swinging (and missing) with the pick.  What should have taken 3 blows
is taking 20, in the meantime i ignore the ant which is slowly killing
me. . .

And which eventually succeeds.

